WHY, BY MY FOUR QUESTIONS
(1) The five pillars: nothing is covert, and the public line gives windows, not dates [AX-0073, AX-0081].
(2) The ramp: 2050-2052 is the demand peak (93% of capacity in 2052), followed by the first steps down. Securing the ramp is the delivery priority whose weight rose in 2026 [AX-0073]. A widebody development in those years would have to bring at least $1B to justify the load, and this one brings +0.58 [AX-0010].
(3) The next generation: I prepare it through the technology roadmap and the Board's off-site, on technology gates and two engine sources, not through a launch [AX-0020, AX-0006].
(4) The Board: it accepts hold, and hold carries no item.

THE GRID
- The A350 Re-engine is +0.58 in S1, my expected column. That is within $1B, so the company default stands.
- It also fails profile section 6 (at least $1B over Do Nothing) and both of my round-3 conditions for this window:
  - no Rolls-Royce widebody engine is on the record (an UltraFan launched now is ready in 2056, a year after entry into service in 2055);
  - the margin is under $1B.
- Every tie-break within $1B favours hold: less concurrency with the peak, a later capex start and fewer Board items.
- Plan-level robustness now favours hold too: worst +11.59 against +11.18.

ON THE RECORD
- I hold to my condition of at least $1B.
- Forgone value: +0.58 in S1-S5, +0.48 on my weights.
- Loss avoided: 0.41 in S6-S7. Break-even is about 59% on S6+S7.
- I say it plainly: this hold closes the A350 Re-engine for the game. It is a doctrine choice, not a forced one.
- I would revisit only if both memos pass the item and show the grid misreads it. I would then record in the rationale why I set the $1B line aside. I do not expect to.

OVERRIDE: none. The game's one override closes unused, which is the outcome the Board prefers.

EXPECTED SCENARIO
- S1, rivals hold, at 45%.
- Weights: S1 45%, S2 20%, S3 10%, S4 10%, S5 5%, S6 5%, S7 5%, unchanged.
- Boeing's line ('stable' widebody lines, no fps date, the business case 'isn't' there) leans away from S6-S7. The bulletin rules out no column.
- S2-S5 are value-neutral for us on this grid. Default +11.62 on these weights; the worst plausible column is S6-S7 at +11.59.

DELAY TACTICS: none, as in every round of this game. Every move would be naked, and it loses in every column.

OTHER MOVES I expect (unpriced):
- a rate plan through the 2052 peak and the step-down to 2060, each step gated on quality KPIs, with the workforce through recruitment and redeployment;
- supply security for our own lines and A320 fleet support with no draw on fleet spares;
