(5) The capacity case for the 2051 step (+74 engines over 2050's 913, and +97 by 2052), priced against Do Nothing and against a buyback at 10%. If Shane says the peak can be met lean, say there is no case. Capacity sized for 1,010 would sit 43% idle by 2060.

